  "quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "I spent 18 months turning my second brain into my living research memory.",
      "timestamp_sec": 0,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=0s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "within my second brain, I currently have over 5,000 notes in Obsidian and another 5,000 notes in Readwise and some scattered in Notion and Google Drive",
      "timestamp_sec": 0,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=0s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "you need a system that sits between those harnesses and your second brain",
      "timestamp_sec": 34,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=34s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "how can we make research better, but more specifically, how can we better leverage what we have?",
      "timestamp_sec": 196,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=196s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "It's not agent native. And it's obviously weak for coding tasks since it's just browser based.",
      "timestamp_sec": 328,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=328s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "But, this needs an infrastructure. It's not really human-friendly to be able to digest quickly, to check notes, to make edits. It's hard to inspect by hand.",
      "timestamp_sec": 381,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=381s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "the next session you use Codex, you have to paste it all again or ask it to use skills.",
      "timestamp_sec": 477,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=477s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "The bottleneck is how can you leverage it in the future? Meaning that with an agent, the context window becomes everything, the database, the file system, the memory, the reasoning space.",
      "timestamp_sec": 516,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=516s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "we don't need necessarily to provide more and more and more context for a better research. You need a proper memory and context management",
      "timestamp_sec": 516,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=516s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "So basically after three rounds of generating six queries per round, we ended up with like 40-50 links in total.",
      "timestamp_sec": 872,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=872s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "For the course, it worked great right away. We generated 35 lessons really quick, but we wanted more.",
      "timestamp_sec": 925,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=925s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "this research MD file is static. It's a pile of static data. And usually research is not static, right?",
      "timestamp_sec": 1063,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=1063s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "It consumes a lot of tokens and it takes a lot of time.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1063,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=1063s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "that's why V3 of this system is actually a deep research algorithm plus an LM knowledge base on top of it, aka the wiki layer.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1100,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=1100s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "you should forget the infra structure you think you need, such as vector databases, knowledge graphs, semantic search, text search.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1144,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=1144s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "So, no database, just a simple index based on references.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1185,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=1185s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "And sometimes the agent just looks into this, gets what it needs, and goes back. Which is very token efficient, right?",
      "timestamp_sec": 1371,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=1371s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "the beautiful part is that this wiki is actually alive, right? For example, every question leaves a trace into your wiki.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1418,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=1418s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Obsidian is just an immutable snapshot that a LLM never touches, right? So, this is my data. I don't really want the LLM to touch my personal notes that I manually write",
      "timestamp_sec": 1499,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=1499s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "The project is the work, and your second brain is the research.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1596,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=1596s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "usually light or fast is more than enough because remember this process consumes a lot of tokens.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1723,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=1723s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "the other main goal of this project is to teach memory and context management",
      "timestamp_sec": 2222,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=2222s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "our goal is to teach AI engineering. It's not to build the next best product.",
      "timestamp_sec": 2257,
      "talk_slug": "turn-10994-notes-into-memory",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZRM_TfEZcIo&t=2257s",
